# [CompliRules] Schrems II International Data Transfer & Transfer Impact Assessment (TIA) Guardrail
**Severity:** `CRITICAL` | **Jurisdiction:** `GDPR_EU`

<!-- NOTICE: CompliRules provides automated AST guardrails under MIT License without warranty (See DISCLAIMER.md). Documentation: https://halilyilmz.github.io/complirules/ -->

## Legal Citations
- **Regulation (EU) 2016/679 (GDPR) (Chapter V (Articles 44-49))**: Transfers of personal data to third countries or international organisations.
- **CJEU Landmark Precedent (Case C-311/18 (Schrems II))**: Standard Contractual Clauses (SCCs) are invalid without supplementary technical measures in surveillance jurisdictions.

## Rule Mandates
- MUST: Perform a documented Transfer Impact Assessment (TIA) before integrating US SaaS services.
- MUST: Verify active EU-US Data Privacy Framework (DPF) certification for all US processors.
- MUST: When using SCCs with US entities, apply supplementary measures: client-side envelope encryption with keys held in the EEA or self-hosted proxy IP scrubbing.

## Forbidden Anti-Patterns
- NEVER: fetch("https://api.mixpanel.com/track", { headers: { "X-Forwarded-For": userIp } })

